  "topPRs": [
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABKBxjaQ",
      "title": "compliance: spec improvements from fma",
      "author": "0xOneTony",
      "number": 977,
      "body": "Spec fixes from the bridge hook FMA review, on top of #971, grouped by failure mode.\r\n\r\n**FM2: Completions publish more deposit gas than one L2 block can take**\r\n- The published deposit gas count covers the whole L1 block in which a hook is set or removed.\r\n\r\n**FM3: A withdrawal calls the hook or the bridge's escrow functions**\r\n- `completeWithdrawalTransaction` reverts if the target is an Unsafe Target at the time of completion.\r\n\r\n**FM9: The policy screens the wrong parties**\r\n- The policy always receives two parties, sender then recipient, decoded only from messages the messengers sent.\r\n- The module reads the L1 bridge and messenger addresses from the Portal's `SystemConfig` when deployed.\r\n- New `parties()` view returns the same two addresses.\r\n\r\n**FM10: A clearance outlives the check it was written for**\r\n- Completion passes the policy the record's `clearedAt`.\r\n\r\n**FM12 / FM17: A compromised policy / a wrong disable cutoff**\r\n- `setPolicy`, `disable` and `enable` emit `PolicySet`, `Disabled` (with the cutoff) and `Enabled`.\r\n\r\n**FM13: The module's balance stops covering what it holds**\r\n- The bridge moves held tokens before the hook records the hold.\r\n\r\n**FM15: Non-standard tokens break holds or completions**\r\n- The module supports ETH, Native L1 Tokens and `OptimismMintableERC20` tokens.\r\n\r\n**FM19: The hook stands between governance and L2**\r\n- `depositTransaction` skips the hook for deposits sent by the ProxyAdmin owner, so governance actions on L2 never wait on screening. The overview's goals note the exception.\r\n\r\nCloses https://github.com/ethereum-optimism/optimism-private/issues/823",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-22T13:08:54Z",
      "mergedAt": null,
      "additions": 40,
      "deletions": 14
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABJ8OmHA",
      "title": "stage-1,deputy-pause-module: name the Foundation Upgrade Safe as the DeputyPauseModule foundation safe",
      "author": "mds1",
      "number": 975,
      "body": "The Stage 1 diagram and the DeputyPauseModule spec name the Foundation Operations Safe (`0x9BA6e03D8B90dE867373Db8cF1A58d2F7F006b3A`) as the Safe that controls the DeputyPauseModule. The live module is configured with the Foundation Upgrade Safe, and it is installed on the Security Council Guardian Safe. The DeputyPauseModule spec's own Overview already says the module is installed on the Guardian Safe.\n\nOn-chain evidence (Ethereum mainnet block 26245754):\n\n```\ncast call 0x09f7150D8c019BeF34450d6920f6B3608ceFdAf2 'getModulesPaginated(address,uint256)(address[],address)' 0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000001 10\n# [0x76fC2F971FB355D0453cF9F64d3F9E4f640E1754]\ncast call 0x76fC2F971FB355D0453cF9F64d3F9E4f640E1754 'foundationSafe()(address)'\n# 0x847B5c174615B1B7fDF770882256e2D3E95b9D92   (Foundation Upgrade Safe)\ncast call 0x76fC2F971FB355D0453cF9F64d3F9E4f640E1754 'guardianSafe()(address)'\n# 0x09f7150D8c019BeF34450d6920f6B3608ceFdAf2   (Guardian Safe)\n```\n\nChanges:\n\n- `stage-1.md`: the `pause` edge to the DeputyPauseModule now starts at the Foundation Upgrade Safe node that the diagram already has.\n- `deputy-pause-module.md`: \"Operations Safe\" becomes \"Foundation Safe\", which matches the `foundationSafe` getter and the existing iDPM-005 and `setDeputy` text. Where the text names the Safe the module runs in, it now says the Security Council Guardian Safe.\n\n`configurability.md` is not changed.\n\nReviewed with Codex (gpt-6-astra, high): no findings.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-22T04:27:36Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-22T16:53:42Z",
      "additions": 9,
      "deletions": 9
    },
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOLB-lzc8AAAABKAQkHA",
      "title": "chore(ci): bump circleci-utils orb to 1.0.33",
      "author": "falcorocks",
      "number": 976,
      "body": "## Summary\n\n- Bumps the ethereum-optimism/circleci-utils orb from 1.0.13 to 1.0.33.\n- circleci-utils 1.0.33 installs mise tools fresh by default (no mise cache) and sets `MISE_RUSTUP_HOME` to the mise data dir. Cargo-backed tools (`mdbook`, `mdbook-katex`, `mdbook-linkcheck`, `mdbook-mermaid`) then failed with \"rustup could not choose a version of cargo\".\n- Pins `RUSTUP_TOOLCHAIN` to the rust version in `mise.toml` (1.83.0) on the `lint-specs` and `build-book` jobs so the cargo installs resolve a toolchain.\n",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/specs",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-22T11:05:23Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-10-22T12:18:34Z",
      "additions": 5,
      "deletions": 1
    }
